WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:02.667
-Welcome back to "Late Night,"
We're here with D'Arcy Carden.

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.434
Um, you know, wonderful cast.

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:06.000
Big cast, famous names.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.000
-I just did the thing
that people do on talk shows

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.767
where I saw myself in the --
I kind of -- I saw myself

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:12.534
and I adjusted.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:14.767
Like, I'm talking to you,
but I'm like -- Oh. Oh.

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.334
-And you know what the funny
thing is?

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:17.834
Everybody watching
could see it.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:18.968
You know what I mean?

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:20.267
Like, I do it, too.
-Yes.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:21.834
-Where you think you're catching
yourself in a mirror,

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:22.934
but you forget it's the thing
everyone sees.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:25.000
-Yes, totally. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.634
-TV, baby.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:27.934
-You were saying?
-And you think,

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.100
"I'll do it really subtly."
-Yeah, nobody will notice

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.133
that I'm, like,
sort of looking like this.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:34.033
And...okay, anyway.
You were saying, sir?

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.467
-What's it like --
Jennifer Lopez, Lenny Kravitz.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:37.501
Who else is in the film?
-Oh, my God.

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:38.801
-What's it like,
that first table read

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:41.267
when you sit down with
those sort of A-list names?

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:44.100
-So, I mean, the cast is insane
because it's Lenny Kravitz

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.067
and it's J.Lo and Sonia Braga,

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:49.100
and it's all these people that
are -- [stammers]

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.467
The table read was insane.

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:52.067
But the funny thing is,
the only thing I can think of

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.767
when I think of the table read
is that is when I met J.Lo.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.667
-Yeah.
-Okay. That's Jennifer Lopez.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:57.667
-Yeah.

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:58.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:00.934
-I -- It was
this big old table read.

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:03.400
I see her come in. You can,
like, feel it when she walks

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.767
into the room.
I can see her come in,

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:05.968
and all of a sudden, I was like,
"Okay, this is going to be

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:07.334
a long table read. I got to --
I got to pee.

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:08.701
I gotta go pee.
I gotta to run and go pee.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.167
-Yep, very smart.
-I can't -- Thank you.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:12.100
-Yeah.
-And that's part of the biz.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.934
-That's why you're good
at the biz.

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.234
-Exactly. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:18.300
So I ran to go pee,
and I open the bathroom door,

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.467
and immediately I'm like,
"Something is up."

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:23.300
And I open the stall
and it's just not good.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.467
-Okay.
-It's bad in there. It's bad.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:26.367
-Someone left it
not the way they found it.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:28.701
-It shouldn't have -- Yes.
Yeah, exactly.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:31.033
It's so bad that I, like,
have to wash my hands

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:32.501
just being in the room.
Yes.

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:34.901
-You saw it and had
to wash your hands.

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:36.334
-I saw it and was like,
"I got to go. I got to go."

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:39.634
I'm washing my hands to leave
and who walks in the door --

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:40.634
[ Audience groans and laughs ]

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:43.334
-Oh, no. Yeah.

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:44.801
Can I call her J.Lo?
Can I say J.Lo?

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:46.000
-Yes, you can. Yeah.
-My guess is J.Lo.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.267
-She did, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.501
-So she walks in the door.
I'm washing my hands,

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:51.601
which is just admitting guilt.
-Oh, yeah. Yeah.

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:53.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:55.667
-And so I, like, run out, and
I run into her security guard,

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:58.634
and I just go,
"It's bad in there."

00:01:58.634 --> 00:01:59.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:00.801
-Good. Good cover.

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:02.067
-Yeah, I don't know.

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:03.701
-And then later you, like,
tried to laugh and cover.

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.801
Be like, "I bet you probably had
to wash your hands

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:07.767
when you saw it,
because that's what I did."

00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:09.567
I washed -- I saw it and...
-I saw it and washed.

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:11.267
-...Washed my hands,
in case you're wondering why.

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:13.100
-I just said that
to everybody near her

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.434
so that she maybe overheard.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.634
Lenny is like, "Why are you
telling me this again?"

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.801
-There's a scene where
all this incredible cast

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:23.834
is shooting in a swimming pool
fully clothed.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.968
-Yes.
-And I don't want to give

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:27.667
anything away from the plot,
but you're forced to be

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:28.801
in the swimming pool
fully clothed.

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:31.567
I would imagine
that is not good times?

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:32.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:35.834
-It's funny, because we're in
the Dominican Republic.

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:37.300
It's so beautiful.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.467
We're shooting in this gorgeous
pool overlooking literally,

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:41.901
like, whales jumping
out of the ocean.

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:44.167
It was so, like, idyllic --
is that how you say it?

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:46.200
-Yeah.
-Idyllic? It was so beautiful.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.868
But we were in the pool
for, like, 20 days.

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:52.567
We were shooting in the pool
for three weeks.

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:54.467
-That's too many days.
-That's too many days.

00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:56.167
What you'll find is three
is too many days.

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:58.167
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Your skin starts reacting

00:02:58.167 --> 00:03:00.434
weird. We had, like,
rashes, like the --

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:02.367
you know, I don't know, maybe
the filter stopped working

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:04.667
at some point.
There's just, like, sunscreen.

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:07.334
So to complain about it is so
silly because it really was

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:11.234
just such a joy, but it was --
our skin -- it was soggy.

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:12.601
It was very soggy.
-Yeah.

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.567
-It was funny to see, like,
Cheech and Lenny,

00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:16.400
who are wearing full, like,
suits, you know,

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.968
like wedding-y attire.

00:03:18.968 --> 00:03:21.267
They -- We'd all be in the water
up to our necks,

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.200
and then they'd be like,
"Okay, that's lunch."

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.300
And just like --
[ Blows raspberries ]

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:28.734
Just, like, trudging out of
the swimming pool,

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:31.634
like, eating their chicken
in soaking wet clothes.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:32.934
Because you could change
into your robe,

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:34.300
but then what are you going
to do?

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.634
Put on your wet suit again?
-That's even worse, right.

00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:36.801
-Worse!
-Just tough it out.

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:38.567
Stay in the wet suit.
-Tough it out, yeah.

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:42.234
-Now, the idea of seeing
Lenny Kravitz of all people,

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:44.534
who -- cool emanates off
this man.

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:47.234
-He like, defines it.
-And to be in a wet suit

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:49.133
eating chicken, that seems --
-I know.

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:52.300
-Like, this should not happen
to a man at his level.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.367
-You, like, have to avert
your eyes.

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:54.501
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.801
-But did you enjoy your time
with Lenny?

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:58.067
-I did.
-Yeah.

00:03:58.067 --> 00:04:00.167
-Yeah, he's great.
-Yeah, and you lived with him.

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:02.801
-We lived together. It was
like -- I mean, he is --

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:05.300
he is just a rockstar.
-By the way, when his wife

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.234
was living with Lenny Kravitz,
I hope Henry Winkler

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:09.100
called up Jason and said,
"You can come stay with us."

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:12.734
"I know this must be a very hard
time for you right now."

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:15.000
-It's the same thing.
It's exactly the same thing.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.267
"You're going through a thing.
Come stay with us.

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:19.367
Clean your teeth."
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:20.434
-Yeah, it was great.

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:23.100
He just is -- it was such
a weird thing,

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.100
living with Lenny Kravitz.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.467
Like, you would be
eating breakfast

00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:28.100
and he would come to
the breakfast table in, like,

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.367
a shirt that was open to here
and, like, leather pants.

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:32.200
-Yeah.
-But we were there for months.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:35.133
So we really -- Everybody --
I know casts always say

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:37.501
we became a family,
but we really did.

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:38.834
-[ Laughs ]
-We really did.

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:40.834
-Yeah. The other people
are posers, but you guys --

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:44.067
-And I've said it before.
-Yeah, and not meant it.

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:46.501
-But you know, it was, like,
a year into COVID.

00:04:46.501 --> 00:04:50.300
I had had no meals with anybody
other than Jason.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.801
There it is.
I finally said his name.

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:52.801
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.
-My husband.

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:54.067
-We got it out there.
-Yeah.

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:56.100
-I had not made a new friend.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.200
You remember that time.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:58.267
-Yeah.
-It was dark.

00:04:58.267 --> 00:04:59.400
And so to have all the --
I don't know.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.934
It was such a bonding
experience.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.901
It was so -- and to live
with each other on top of it

00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:05.801
was just, like, insane.
It was so great.

00:05:05.801 --> 00:05:08.367
-Well, that's really fun.
Congratulations on the film.

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:09.901
It's always so lovely
to have you here.

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:10.901
-I love ya.
-Thank you so much.

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:13.601
You guys, that's D'Arcy Carden.

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:15.968
"Shotgun Wedding" is streaming
now on Prime Video.

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:17.968
We'll be back
with more "Late Night."

